Make the "git" flavor of the client a shell package nexora patches.

Three things about this tree are not what nexora wants: two of them are
megabytes of dead weight in the APK, one of them loads a second copy of a
plugin manager at startup.

CMake's if(ANDROID) block stages ~26 MB of 3rdparty/cs16client-extras, yapb
configs and downloaded bot graphs into android/app/src/main/assets, and gradle
packages all of it. Nexora ships the game content as its own game-assets.zip
release asset and installs it into the game directory, so the APK carries a
second copy that nothing reads. Emptied, and the graph download moves into the
desktop branch so yapb_graph_dl.py stops reaching out to the network at
configure time on a build whose only job is producing a shell.

The externalNativeBuild block then builds the client, the menu and the server
and packages every one of them: libclient is 6.5 MB and libmenu 6.3 MB per ABI.
Nexora injects its own build of both into this package after download (the
patch log shows "+ libclient_android_arm64.so"). The engine looks for the menu
as cl_dlls/libmenu_android_<arch>.so, then <gamelibdir>/libmenu_android_<arch>.so,
then libmenu.so from its own package - never a copy inside the client APK - and
the client dll is dlopen'ed out of the injected set. yapb and ReGameDLL_CS land
in the build graph but in neither the APK nor nexora's Android bundle.

MainActivity hands the engine "-dll @yapb", which loads the vanilla YaPB
bootstrap. Nexora's bundle ships metamod as the -dll with the bot plugin
alongside it, so the engine has to be pointed at @metamod instead - otherwise it
loads a second, unmanaged copy of the same loader and they fight over the
dll list.

Also: only the arm ABIs, since an x86 install never got a cl_dll from anywhere;
useLegacyPackaging, because the injected .so files are dlopen'ed straight out of
the APK; and minSdk 21 -> 24, matching the API level nexora injects against, so
the APK does not install on a device that cannot load what gets injected into it.

android/ci/build-amxx.sh builds the real libclient/libmenu for the bundles, from
this same pinned tree.

Applied by the "Build the client APK" step, so it is tied to the commit in
cs16-client.pin rather than to a fork of it.

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index c80b503..92dd69b 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -92,6 +92,19 @@ endif()
 
 set(GRAPHS_OUTPUT "${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}/graphs")
 
+if(ANDROID)
+	# Nothing to stage. Nexora ships the game content and installs the bot
+	# graphs from its own bundle, so this APK is a shell that carries no
+	# assets at all. Left in place, the copy below fills
+	# android/app/src/main/assets with ~26 MB of cs16client-extras, yapb
+	# configs and graphs, and gradle packages every byte of it into the APK.
+	#
+	# Moving the graph download into the desktop branch also means
+	# yapb_graph_dl.py never runs here. It reaches out to the network at
+	# configure time, which was pure wall-clock on a build whose only job is
+	# producing a shell package.
+else()
+
 execute_process(
 	COMMAND ${Python_EXECUTABLE}
 	${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/scripts/yapb_graph_dl.py
@@ -101,18 +114,6 @@ execute_process(
 set(EXTRAS_DIR "${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/3rdparty/cs16client-extras")
 set(YAPB_DIR "${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/3rdparty/yapb/cfg")
 
-if(ANDROID)
-	set(EXTRAS_OUTPUT "${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/android/app/src/main/assets")
-
-	file(GLOB EXTRAS_FILES "${EXTRAS_DIR}/*")
-	file(GLOB YAPB_FILES "${YAPB_DIR}/*" "${GRAPHS_OUTPUT}/*")
-
-	file(REMOVE_RECURSE ${EXTRAS_OUTPUT})
-	file(
-		COPY ${EXTRAS_FILES} ${YAPB_FILES}
-		DESTINATION ${EXTRAS_OUTPUT}
-	)
-else()
 	set(EXTRAS_OUTPUT "${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}/extras.pk3")
 
 	execute_process(
diff --git a/android/app/build.gradle b/android/app/build.gradle
index 016139f..0f4b6d5 100644
--- a/android/app/build.gradle
+++ b/android/app/build.gradle
@@ -13,7 +13,7 @@ android {
 		applicationId = "su.xash.cs16client"
 		versionName = "1.35-" + getGitHash()
 		versionCode = getBuildNum()
-		minSdk = 21
+		minSdk = 24
 		targetSdk = 36
 
 		ndk {
@@ -97,6 +97,31 @@ android {
 		create("git") {
 			dimension = "version"
 			buildConfigField("Boolean", "IS_GOOGLE_PLAY_BUILD", "false")
+
+			// Without an abiFilters block AGP builds every ABI the NDK
+			// supports, so the APK carried lib/x86 and lib/x86_64 copies of
+			// the client that nothing can load. Nexora only ever produced
+			// the arm64-v8a and armeabi-v7a bundles, so an x86 install
+			// never got a cl_dll from anywhere.
+			ndk {
+				abiFilters "arm64-v8a", "armeabi-v7a"
+			}
+
+			packaging {
+				jniLibs {
+					// useLegacyPackaging stores .so uncompressed, which is
+					// what the engine needs for the libraries nexora injects
+					// into this package: they are dlopen'ed straight out of
+					// the APK, so extractNativeLibs=false has to stay.
+					useLegacyPackaging = true
+				}
+			}
+
+			externalNativeBuild {
+				cmake {
+					arguments "-DBUILD_CLIENT=OFF", "-DBUILD_SERVER=OFF", "-DBUILD_MAINUI=OFF"
+				}
+			}
 		}
 	}
 
